WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.225
Hi, I'm Turbo!

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:05.343
These low-bit quants claim their bits were placed by measurement.

00:00:05.343 --> 00:00:06.590
Let's check the files.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:13.002
Measure which parts matter, then spend a memory budget where it counts.

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:22.907
Crush one group of tensors at a time, and measure its KL

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:24.104
divergence from full precision.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:28.390
Then allocate bits to minimise KL within the target machine's memory.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.326
Each tensor's type is written in the header, readable without the weights.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:38.226
The toolkit's own chart: lower KL than uniform quants at the same

00:00:38.226 --> 00:00:41.637
size, on a small dense model and a forty-expert mixture.

00:00:42.057 --> 00:00:46.287
The bigger claim is on the mixture: twenty-one to forty-three percent lower KL.

00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:49.866
But this model is dense, and neither chart is this release.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.748
In the largest file, every block gets the same type.

00:00:54.748 --> 00:00:55.722
No per-layer structure.

00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:59.971
In the three smaller files, blocks zero, one, sixty-three and sixty-four

00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:01.363
keep the primary type.

00:01:01.363 --> 00:01:04.844
Blocks two to sixty-two crush their gate and up weights.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.040
Same keep-set at three budgets.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.013
A knapsack re-solved per budget would not normally do that; a first-and-last rule would.

00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:18.342
Demoting attention keys and values saves eleven megabytes of seven point three

00:01:18.342 --> 00:01:21.030
four gigabytes, from the most sensitive tensors.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.874
Demoting the feed-forward gate and up saves seven hundred and sixty-five megabytes.

00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:27.348
That's the real lever.

00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:31.177
No file weighs what its name says.

00:01:31.177 --> 00:01:34.966
The one named one point seven five measures one point nine oh

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.124
six: its output head alone is thirteen point four percent.

00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:42.805
The filename is marketing; the tensor-info block at the top of the

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:43.902
file is the build.

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.536
To recap: measure, fit, then check the header.

00:01:49.536 --> 00:01:50.976
The header is the build.

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:53.863
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:54.443
I'm Turbo.

00:01:54.443 --> 00:01:54.734
Bye!
